Say what a label is told it needs.

The weekday label in the Money Manager Ex New Transaction dialog reads Wednesda, and cocotron 0143
established that the string measures 65.00 while the draw is handed a rect 64.00 wide. The
remaining question was whether the toolkit ever asked us for a width at all.

-[NSTextFieldCell cellSize] is the one place to ask that, because -sizeToFit,
-[NSControl intrinsicContentSize] and -[NSView fittingSize] all funnel through it. One trace there
covers every route.

MEASURED: 56 cellSize calls on that drive, and EVERY ONE of them is on a cell whose string is
empty, answering 1.00 for the string width. Not one is for the weekday, or for any other text.

So wx never asks our cell how wide that label should be, and the 68 point control the text is drawn
into, which is the 64 point rect plus the two point inset on each side, is arrived at by its own
arithmetic. Nothing we answer is wrong here: cocotron 0143 showed the measurement is 65 and
correct, the commit after it showed our size and draw insets agree on 4, and this shows the size
was never requested.

That closes the question of whether the truncation is ours. It does not say what wx does instead,
which is the next thing to find and is on the wx side of the line.

The trace is alive on 56 calls, which is what makes the absence of the weekday worth reading at
all.

